# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — north-star contractile for hermeneia
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell <j.d.a.jewell@open.ac.uk>
#
# Paired runner: intend.ncl
# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become. Two sections share one file because they answer
#            the same question at different ranges:
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done |
#                                    deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → achieved |
#                                    abandoned
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See the `must`
#            contractile for hard gates.

@abstract:
North-star contractile for Hermeneia: the voking / imminence query language for
Vocarium. Hermeneia calls trope-shaped stored particulars into a declared
use-relation and reports what is preserved, lost, licensed, or insufficient
under a use-model — separating the retrieved from the interpretable from the
licensed.

This file was inherited from hermeneia and at instantiation (issue #8)
still declared that this repository IS the canonical RSR template providing "the
scaffold that all hyperpolymath repos should copy". A self-name substitution
fixed the name and left the claim, which is the worse outcome: a north-star
contractile describing a different project. Rewritten from README.adoc,
EXPLAINME.adoc and descriptiles/{STATE,ECOSYSTEM}.a2ml. All three committed
next-action probes below were also FALSE against this tree while two were
declared in_progress and one done; each is restated with a probe that was
executed before it was written down.
@end

## Purpose

Hermeneia is the query layer of the hyperpolymath voking stack. Vocarium stores
vokeable particulars (tropes, transformation paths, grades, warrants, use-models,
verdicts); Haec records transformations; Hermeneia asks what a stored particular
can become under a declared use.

It is organised around a family of voke operations — invoke, evoke, convoke,
transvoke, provoke, intervoke, revoke — of which `invoke` is implemented and
executing end to end against the real trope-checker oracle. The chain is
`query -> Trope IR -> tropecheck -> verdict / witness / coordinate`.

## Anti-Purpose

Sourced from EXPLAINME §10 and ECOSYSTEM.a2ml `what-this-is-not` — the
boundary-erosion guard. This repository is NOT:

- SQL with poetic verbs
- a general-purpose search engine
- a thesaurus
- a semantic oracle or truth engine
- a replacement for human interpretation
- a proof that an answer is good
- the store (that is Vocarium) or the transformation language (that is Haec).
  Hermeneia queries; it does not take long-term storage responsibility and does
  not re-implement transformation effects as query verbs.
- a re-implementation of the trope algebra. trope-checker exposes
  `tropecheck-rs` as a library with `grade_le`, and hermeneia DEPENDS on that
  validated implementation. Reimplementing the algebra here is rejected
  permanently (STATE.a2ml, resolved 2026-07-28).

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask. Sensitive areas:

- `docs/SPEC.adoc` — the specification and its "Status — no overclaim" section.
  A change that widens a claim has to widen the receipts in the same PR.
- `src/hermeneia-ir/` — the Trope IR is the contract with the external oracle;
  changing its shape changes what tropecheck will accept.
- `.machine_readable/contractiles/` and `.machine_readable/descriptiles/` —
  the normative set-point and the descriptive self-model. Coaptation compares
  the two, so editing one without the other is drift, not a change.
- `.machine_readable/configs/instantiation.a2ml` — the values this repository
  was rendered from. Edit it and re-run `just init`; do not hand-edit the
  rendered files.

## Committed Next-Actions

### repo-initialization
- description: The repository is instantiated from its template, and stays so
- probe: bash scripts/instantiate.sh --check
- status: done
- notes: |
    Was "Provide just copy-and-substitute template for new repos" with probe
    `test -f scripts/init-repo.sh`, declared done. No such script has ever
    existed here, so the probe was FALSE against a clause marked complete.
    For an instantiated repo the same clause name means the opposite direction:
    not "can be copied FROM" but "was rendered, and has not drifted back".
    `scripts/instantiate.sh` renders from
    `.machine_readable/configs/instantiation.a2ml` and `--check` exits non-zero
    if any token came back. Also gated by openssf-compliance.yml and by the
    Mustfile's instantiation-rendered invariant.

### contractile-completeness
- description: Every RSR contractile verb has an a2ml declaration and an ncl runner
- probe: test "$(ls .machine_readable/contractiles/*/*.a2ml | wc -l)" -ge 12 && test "$(ls .machine_readable/contractiles/*/*.ncl | wc -l)" -ge 6
- status: done
- notes: |
    The old probe globbed `.machine_readable/contractiles/*.a2ml` — the FLAT
    layout — which matches only INDEX.a2ml here, so it counted 1 and could never
    equal 6. This repo uses the per-verb directory layout (intend/, must/,
    trust/, adjust/, bust/, dust/), which the Mustfile's
    bust-dust-files-present invariant already assumed. Six verbs, each with an
    a2ml declaration plus a manifest a2ml, plus the ncl runner and k9 wrapper.

### automation-scripts
- description: The Justfile's imported phase modules exist, so `just` recipes are not silent no-ops
- probe: test -f build/just/init.just
- status: in_progress
- notes: |
    The old probe counted `^# ` lines in the Justfile and asked whether the count
    matched `[6-9][0-9]*`. The Justfile has 150 such lines, so the probe was
    FALSE — and it measured comment volume, which is not "every repetitive task
    has a recipe".
    The real exposure this repo has is the opposite of too few recipes: the root
    Justfile `import?`s build/just/{init,container,groove,assess}.just and
    build/contractile.just, and `import?` is an OPTIONAL import, so a missing
    module is silently ignored. Only init.just exists (added for issue #8). The
    probe asserts the one that matters; the other four remain absent and are
    recorded in STATE.a2ml rather than papered over by a probe that passes.

## Wishes

### Near Horizon

#### cross-repo-validation
- description: Tooling to validate all repos against RSR spec
- horizon: near
- status: declared

#### automated-substitution
- description: Script to automate repo-specific substitution
- horizon: near
- status: achieved
- notes: |
    Promoted from a wish: scripts/instantiate.sh plus
    .machine_readable/configs/instantiation.a2ml, added for issue #8. Idempotent,
    guard-aware, and gated in CI. What is still wished for is the upstream
    equivalent landing here — build/just/repo-init.just's archetype overlays and
    provenance/deed splicing — which only matters if this repo is ever re-minted
    from a newer template.

### Mid Horizon

